  "content": {
    "title": "Alabama vs Hofstra score, highlights: Crimson Tide advance in March Madness",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 5:44 p.m. ETBe sure to follow USA TODAY Sports' live updates keeping track of all of NCAA Tournament's Friday first round games.No. 4 seed Alabama pulled away late in the second half to defeat No. 13 seed Hofstra in the first round of the NCAA Tournament on Friday, March 20.The Crimson Tide, without starting guard Aden Holloway, only led Hofstra 37-35 at halftime, but outscored the Pride 53-35 in the second half to secure their 90-70 win. Star guard Labaron Philon Jr. was outstanding, scoring 29 points with eight rebounds and seven assists.Hofstra, in its first NCAA Tournament appearance since 2001, ran out of gas late despite its 3-point shooting keeping it within reach for most of the game. The Pride cut Alabama's lead to five with under 10 minutes left in the second half, before the Crimson Tide ultimately took over the game.Alabama now moves to the second round for the fourth consecutive season under coach Nate Oats, and it'll face No. 5 Texas Tech for a spot in the Sweet 16.USA TODAY Sports provided highlights and updates from Alabama's NCAA Tournament win over Hofstra. Follow along.HIT REFRESH FOR LIVE UPDATES.Alabama vs Hofstra live scoreThis section will be updated.TEAMS1H2HFHofstra353570Alabama375390Alabama vs Hofstra live updatesThis section will be updated live. Alabama pulls away late, wins 90-70Alabama outscores Hofstra 53-35 in the second half to exit the first round with a 90-70 win. The Crimson Tide will face No. 5 seed Texas Tech in the second round on Sunday, March 22.Labaron Philon Jr. was outstanding, scoring 29 points with eight rebounds and seven assists in the win. Hofstra sticking aroundHofstra isn't folding over, as it trails Alabama 74-66 with 3:55 left in the second half. Preston Edmead leads the Pride with 21 points on 8-of-21 shooting.Labaron Philon Jr. is having a huge second half, and is up to 26 points with eight rebounds and five assists so far. Alabama pulling awayAlabama is starting to pull away, as it leads Hofstra 59-48 at the under-12 media timeout. Labaron Philon Jr. is causing all sorts of problems for the Pride, as the star guard is up to 19 points with six rebounds and five assists, along with a pair of steals. Alabama comes out of halftime on fireAlabama is starting to pull away early in the second half, having made 4-of-5 shots to take a 47-39 lead early in the period. Labaron Philon Jr. is up to 13 points with four rebounds and four assists, although he has four turnovers. Alabama regains lead before halftimeAlabama leads Hofstra 37-35 at halftime, deleting a 10-point deficit. Aiden Sherrell leads all scorers with 12 points, also using his size advantage with eight rebounds. Labaron Philon Jr. and Taylor Bol Bowen have eight points each.Three-point shooting is keeping Hofstra in the game, as the Pride has made 6-of-13 from distance so far. Hofstra leads 28-18Hofstra extends its lead to 28-18 on another 3-pointer, this time from Joshua Aaron Reaves. The Pride already have five 3-point makes and are shooting 58% from the field early.Alabama is 7-of-20 shooting and 2-of-11 on 3-pointers with 8:55 left in the first half. Hofstra takes 20-16 lead after 8-0 runHere comes Hofstra, which takes a 20-16 lead with 11:06 remaining in the first half following an 8-0 run. The Pride has forced a pair of turnovers from Labaron Philon Jr., both of which have led to points on the other end.Hofstra has already made four 3-pointers, three of which by leading scorer Cruz Davis and German Plotnikov. Alabama hasn't scored in nearly three minutes. Taylor Bol Bowen giving spark off the benchTaylor Bol Bowen is giving Alabama an offensive spark off the bench, hitting a 3-pointer before making a layup as he was fouled. He'll shoot a free throw after the TV timeout, looking to extend Alabama's lead to 14-9 with 14:54 left in the half. Alabama takes early leadAlabama is flexing its muscles early against Hofstra, as it leads 8-2 after three minutes of regulation, forcing a Pride timeout. The Crimson Tide has two steals already, and Philon leads all scorers with four points. Alabama starting lineup vs HofstraHere's a look at Alabama's starting lineup vs. Hofsta without Aden Holloway:G Labaron Philon Jr.G Latrell WrightsellF Amari AllenF London JemisonF Aiden Sherrell Alabama-Hofstra start time pushed backAlabama-Hofstra is being pushed back to a 3:21 p.m. ET tipoff in Tampa, Florida. Fans will have to wait a whopping six extra minutes before the first-round game gets underway.What time does Alabama vs Hofstra start?Time: 3:21 p.m. ETDate: Friday, March 20Alabama-Hofstra is set for a 3:15 p.m. ET tipoff on Friday, March 20, from Benchmark International Arena in Tampa, Florida.How to watch Alabama vs Hofstra today: What channel is Alabama vs Hofstra on?TV channel: truTVStreaming: March Madness Live | Sling TVAlabama-Hofstra will air live on truTV and can be streamed with March Madness Live (with a TV provider login) or Sling TV, which carries truTV and other Turner network TV channels.Alabama vs Hofstra predictionEhsan Kassim: HofstraJohn Leuzzi: AlabamaCraig Meyer: AlabamaJordan Mendoza: AlabamaAlabama vs Hofstra oddsOdds provided by BetMGMMoneyline: Alabama (-750) | Hofstra (+525)Spread: Alabama (-12.5)O/U total: 159.5Why isn't Aden Holloway playing for Alabama?Holloway will miss at least the first weekend of the NCAA Tournament for Alabama after he was arrested March 16 on two felony counts related to possessing 2.1 pounds of marijuana in his residence.Alabama coach Nate Oats declined to comment if Holloway could return, should Alabama advance to the Sweet 16. Read more on Holloway's status here.",
